        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "How the sales-led motion began",
            "content": "When Annie Pearl joined, Calendly’s ARR was 99% PLG and it had just hired its first CRO to build a sales team. The motion grew out of product usage: signups often spread virally, solo users invited teammates, and when a team began using Calendly, its leader might inbound or be identified through product-qualified-lead data. Sales then contacted that team lead about expanding Calendly across the organization. Pearl said the sales-led segment later represented about 20% of ARR and was the fastest-growing segment at that time.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1",
              "S3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Reps suited to the early approach",
            "content": "Because leads were often inbound or PQLs with evidence of team usage, the early sales motion called for reps comfortable with that kind of selling—not necessarily outbound-heavy hunters. Pearl said prior background and the type of selling a candidate had done mattered more than personality type. The target buyer was typically a department head, such as a head of sales, revenue operations, or recruiting, rather than a senior IT buyer or CIO.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1",
              "S2"
            ]
          }
